{"type":"standard","title":"Don Tracy","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Don Tracy</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q107427071","titles":{"canonical":"Don_Tracy","normalized":"Don Tracy","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Don Tracy</span></span>"},"pageid":68014011,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1368140146","tid":"117f4d9d-922b-11f1-948c-f2643f5992b5","timestamp":"2026-08-07T06:41:50Z","description":"American lawyer and politician (born 1949/50)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Don_Tracy","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Don_Tracy?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Don_Tracy?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Don_Tracy"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Don_Tracy","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Don_Tracy","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Don_Tracy?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Don_Tracy"}},"extract":"Don Tracy is an American lawyer, Republican politician, and business owner. Tracy served as acting and confirmed chair of the Illinois Gaming Board (2015–2019), an appointee of then-Governor Bruce Rauner, and as chair of the Illinois Republican Party (2021–2024), succeeding Tim Schneider. He ran unsuccessfully as a candidate for Lieutenant Governor in his state's 2010 general election. He is the Republican nominee in the 2026 United States Senate election in Illinois.","extract_html":"<p><b>Don Tracy</b> is an American lawyer, Republican politician, and business owner. Tracy served as acting and confirmed chair of the Illinois Gaming Board (2015–2019), an appointee of then-Governor Bruce Rauner, and as chair of the Illinois Republican Party (2021–2024), succeeding Tim Schneider. He ran unsuccessfully as a candidate for Lieutenant Governor in his state's 2010 general election. He is the Republican nominee in the 2026 United States Senate election in Illinois.</p>"}